    <item>
      <title>Oat – Ultra-lightweight, semantic, zero-dependency HTML UI component library</title>
      <link>https://oat.ink/</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Oat is an ultra-lightweight HTML + CSS, semantic UI component library with zero dependencies. Native elements like &lt;button&gt;, &lt;input&gt;, &lt;dialog&gt; and semantic attributes like role="button" are styled directly. Proper keyboard navigation support for all components and elements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47021980"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HN Discussion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://oat.ink/'&gt;Read Original Article&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top 11 Comments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;yoz-y:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Claims no classes but uses data- attributes and also classes (just look at the button example…)&lt;p&gt;Looks okay, but I don’t see why to use this over something like Marx if all you need is to not have bare browser default styling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maxion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;This looks very very cool. Will definitely look in to using this for more static internal tools!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;scandinavian:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;5 day old repo, 2000 stars on GitHub, 400 total weekly downloads on npm. Frontpage of hacker news with a bunch of weird comments. Moderation has been lacking recently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;koakuma-chan:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;This is kind of misleading. It says it&amp;#x27;s an HTML UI library, then it says HTML + CSS, and then it says it also includes JavaScript. Why is this better than, say, DaisyUI?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;jlg23:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;My initial reaction was that I have to use this just because of the buzzword density in the title. But after reading up, it looks like the author was pretty successful in moving the bloat from code to announcement title. I&amp;#x27;ll give this a try!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;rado:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Good one. Presentation is good too. Thanks&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;andrei_says_:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Thank you for this, can’t wait to use. Minimalism at its best.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;kitd:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Great work! PicoCSS feels a bit &lt;i&gt;too&lt;/i&gt; minimalist at times.  This looks like a better balance of lightweight and functional.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;deafpolygon:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;I love it. We need to see more of this.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;bpev:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Amazing! I recently started building something similar for the same reasons, but more out of frustration rather than out of desire. I&amp;#x27;ll have to give this one a try and see if it fills the need.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;neon_me:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Nice job! Clicked tru my obscure mobile firefox and all worked well!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://oat.ink/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 15 Feb 2026 08:17:05 +0000</pubDate>
